Docker image runtime components  (installed at build time, not vendored here)
  The image built from Dockerfile pulls ROS 2 Humble and a GStreamer video
  stack from the Ubuntu and ROS archives. GStreamer core and its base/good/bad
  plugin sets are LGPL-2.1-or-later; gstreamer1.0-libav wraps FFmpeg, which
  Ubuntu packages under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

  gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly is deliberately NOT installed. It is unnecessary
  for the H.264/H.265 decode path used by siyi_camera_node (which needs only
  decodebin plus avdec_h26x from libav) and it carries additional codec
  licensing obligations. Do not add it without checking that trade-off.
